# Presence rendering

Draw one presence. The primary file is `female-executive.glb`. Keep its materials. Play Idle before the mesh becomes visible. Drive the mouth from viseme morph targets. `jawOpen` is not the lip-sync channel. The Microsoft mesh and `sampleFigure` are fallbacks only when that file fails. Do not draw a video or a sprite sheet. Do not mirror the mesh.

- Palette: background `#101419`, particles `#B5D7D2`, `#DCEAF0`, `#5E859A`, highlights `#E5C89D`.
- High, medium, and low tiers change the pixel ratio. A measured frame rate below 24 selects low.
- `digitalHumanComplete` stays false until unique clips and mesh variants exist.
- Label simulated homes as simulation. A missing WebGL context leaves the text conversation in place.

Do not add a neon bloom pass or a second full-screen post effect. Do not describe this export as a finished character.
